WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.960
- It's amazing to see
everybody come together

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.830
each October to support
breast cancer awareness.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.410
But there's one athlete who went way past

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.540
just wearing pink.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.650
Look at this post about
former running back

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.560
DeAngelo Williams.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.680
In honor of his mom and several aunts

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.890
who died from breast cancer,

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.930
he paid for mammograms for 500 women,

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.533
and he doesn't plan on stopping, y'all.

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:22.600
(applause)

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.893
We've got DeAngelo on Skype right now!

00:00:24.893 --> 00:00:26.613
What's up DeAngelo?

00:00:26.613 --> 00:00:30.113
(cheering)
Hi, I'm Kelly!

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.260
Okay, so first of all,
you are a great man.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.370
Like, just a great example of a man.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.448
Thank you so much first of all for that.

00:00:38.448 --> 00:00:40.280
(applause)

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.580
And tell us a bit about your foundation.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.393
- So, my foundation started in 2006.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:50.710
That's when obviously I got
drafted and stuff like that.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.620
My four aunts and mom all
carried the BRCA1 gene,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.090
and after 2006,

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.020
I'd already lost three aunts

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:00.980
to the breast cancer.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.330
And then in 2014 I lost my mom

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.600
and my other aunt before that.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.336
So I lost my four aunts
and my mom to it, so--

00:01:09.336 --> 00:01:10.728
- That is just devastating.

00:01:10.728 --> 00:01:12.015
- Because I lost them to that disease,

00:01:12.015 --> 00:01:15.810
I started this because I
didn't want anybody else

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.920
to feel the way that I felt.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.270
So in 2014, we started
the 53 Strong for my mom.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.820
She was 53 years old and
we give those mammograms

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.740
and that's how we ultimately hit 500.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.702
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:28.702 --> 00:01:29.535
(cheers and applause)

00:01:29.535 --> 00:01:32.400
So how do you feel about finally reaching

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.490
the 500 mammograms?

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:35.323
How's that make you feel?

00:01:35.323 --> 00:01:36.965
That's a big goal!

00:01:36.965 --> 00:01:38.280
- Well, it is.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.390
I feel pretty good, but I'm not there yet,

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.580
where I wanna be in terms of,

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.780
you know I wanna save every
life that I possibly can.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.870
But at the same time, I
don't know if you know this,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.077
but there's no camera when
we do stuff like this,

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:55.280
'cause I don't do this for
clicks, likes, or follows.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.190
I do this to save lives, (applause)

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.661
'cause I don't want anybody to experience

00:01:58.661 --> 00:02:00.403
what I've experienced.

00:02:00.403 --> 00:02:02.923
(cheering)

00:02:02.923 --> 00:02:04.920
- You're a very good man.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.494
What's next for you and the foundation?

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:11.080
- Well, this is my ultimate goal.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.800
We've given mammograms
in four different states.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.100
We wanna do it all 50
states simultaneously,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.760
and go overseas and do it as well.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.400
I wanna leave this world better

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.953
than what it was when I found it.

00:02:24.953 --> 00:02:25.786
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:02:25.786 --> 00:02:28.820
- That's the reason why I
do the things that I do,

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.840
and on top of that, there's no formality

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.010
in terms of how much mammograms cost.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:35.930
Like a mammogram in North Carolina

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.470
could be twice as much as a
mammogram in Pennsylvania.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.660
So there's no set price for a mammogram,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.810
so that's my ultimate
goal is to give fifty

00:02:45.139 --> 00:02:48.370
"53 Strong for Sandra" mammograms,

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.223
all 50 states, and in the world.

00:02:51.223 --> 00:02:52.056
(applause)

00:02:52.056 --> 00:02:55.890
- Well, I'm gonna support this
as much as I possibly can.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.660
I thank you so much for all that you do.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.210
I'm so sorry you went through all

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.020
the devastating loss in your life,

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.410
but what you're doing with that loss

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.080
in turning it around and
trying to be positive

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.330
is an amazing thing so thank you so much.

